(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[5 1 "// Frames and threads (doc/python/PYI-SPEC.md §7.4; PYS7 (a)): a frame is a heap object holding a code"] [6 1 "// object's locals, cells, value stack and instruction index; the dispatch loop (eval.go) runs a"] [7 1 "// thread's frames without holding them on Go's stack, so a call from Python to Python is a new frame"] [8 1 "// and a return pops it, and a generator (PY5d) is a frame kept between resumptions."] [10 1 "// Frame is an executing code object (CPython's _PyInterpreterFrame and frame object)."] [13 21 "// the function run, nil for a module's or class's body"] [16 17 "// the namespace of a module's or class's body (a module's is its Globals)"] [17 2 "// LocalsMap is a class body's namespace when __prepare__ returned a dict subclass: the name"] [18 2 "// operations go through its __getitem__, __setitem__ and __delitem__ (CPython's STORE_NAME on a"] [19 2 "// non-exact dict), Locals its dict. Added by PY5e as the integration's owner (part 2b: enum's"] [20 2 "// EnumDict)."] [22 21 "// the fast locals; nil is unbound"] [23 21 "// the cells, then the free variables' cells"] [25 16 "// the next instruction"] [26 16 "// the instruction running, or the last run (f_lasti; tracebacks' line)"] [28 2 "// Suspended is set by a yield (PY5d): the frame returned a value but is kept to be resumed."] [30 17 "// the loop returns when this frame returns: it was called from Go"] [33 1 "// FrameType is the frame objects' type (sys._getframe, a traceback's tb_frame)."] [38 1 "// Line is the frame's current line (f_lineno), 0 when the code has no lines."] [53 1 "// popN pops n items and returns them in stack order (a view, valid until the next push)."] [64 1 "// Thread is a Python thread's state (PyThreadState): its current frame, the exception being"] [65 1 "// handled (sys.exception()), the call depth against the recursion limit. One thread runs at a time"] [66 1 "// (the GIL: PYS10 (a), PY6)."] [70 17 "// the exception being handled a